    "description": "Vintage Glass Insulators Lot - 7 Pieces\nHemingray, Whitall Tatum Co., Made in USA\nClear and Aqua Glass, Early to Mid-20th Century\nCollection of seven vintage glass telegraph and telephone insulators, featuring examples from prominent American manufacturers including Hemingray and Whitall Tatum. These utilitarian objects were essential components of the nation's early telecommunications infrastructure, and today they are highly collectible for their industrial aesthetic and varying glass tones.\nPieces Included:\nHemingray - 9 insulator, light aqua glass, embossed mark on base\nWhitall Tatum Co. insulator, clear glass, embossed base mark\nMade in USA insulator, clear glass, marked 21-52\nMade in USA insulator, clear glass, marked 28\nThree (3) additional Made in USA insulators, clear glass, various sizes\nCondition:\nOverall very good vintage condition. Most pieces show typical base roughness and small fleabites consistent with industrial use and age. No significant structural cracks. The glass remains largely clear with some minor surface soot or mineral deposits from outdoor exposure.\nOverall Condition\n: All items are USED and are sold AS-IS. Please open a ticket for any questions prior to bidding.\nUsed Item Description\n: Used condition indicates item(s) show signs of regular use, age and may have had repairs or may need repairs. All items featured are DONATED and all sales are FINAL. All BIDS are placed by the buyer with the understanding that this is a donated item that may contain faults unseen by our staff and is ultimately SOLD AS-IS as all information is presented. Items come strictly as pictured and should be assumed to be AS-IS with possible unseen defects. We are\nNOT\nexperts in any field.",
